# Local tool state. Tailwind v4's automatic source detection scans every
# non-ignored file in the project for class names, so a notes file that merely
# mentions a utility class silently injects that rule into the built CSS.
# (Confirmed: these notes were the source of a stray rule in the bundle.)
.workbuddy-ai/

# Extra git worktrees live here. Git does not honour an ignore rule for a
# registered worktree path, but Tailwind skips the nested repo anyway.
.kilo/

